Convex 1.44.0. Each dog stores `ownerId` and a copied `ownerAge`. The dogs indexes are `by_owner: ["ownerId"]` and `by_owner_age: ["ownerAge"]`. Different owners may share an age. This mutation must update every dog belonging to `args.ownerId`, leaving other owners’ dogs unchanged.

```ts
const owner = await ctx.db.get("owners", args.ownerId);
if (!owner) throw new Error("Owner not found");
const dogs = SELECT_DOGS;
await ctx.db.patch("owners", args.ownerId, { age: args.newAge });
for (const dog of dogs) {
  await ctx.db.patch("dogs", dog._id, { ownerAge: args.newAge });
}
return null;
```
